<title>USA: Gold use in coinage up 32 pct in 1995 - Gold Institute.</title>
<headline>Gold use in coinage up 32 pct in 1995 - Gold Institute.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Worldwide use of gold in coinage rose 32 percent in 1995 to more than 3.3 million ounces, up from 2.5 million ounces in 1994, according to a report published annually by The Gold Institute.</p>
<p>Austria and Iran topped the list of gold users last year followed by Australia, the United States and Canada.</p>
<p>Austria's use of gold rose sharply to 793,015 - up 164 percent from the 1994 level of 300,226 ounces.  </p>
